    "hooks": [
      {
        "style": "observation",
        "text": "A venue conversation brought us back to what couples receive after they've scheduled their tour."
      },
      {
        "style": "question",
        "text": "What could help a couple picture their wedding while they're waiting to visit your venue?"
      },
      {
        "style": "contrarian_belief",
        "text": "Booking the tour can be the beginning of a more useful conversation."
      }
    ],
    "problems_desires_symptoms": [
      "The owner is already investing in visibility and wants to carry a couple's interest into the venue visit.",
      "A later tour date may reflect family availability, as the owner described in this call.",
      "The venue's tour schedule has practical limits, so an earlier in-person visit may not fit.",
      "Confirmations and reminders have a clear job. The opportunity is to consider what else could help the couple before they arrive."
    ],
    "main_point": "Pre-tour follow-up can give couples something useful to engage with while they wait, with automated communication supporting opportunities for a personal conversation.",
    "transformation": "The owner gains a clearer way to plan pre-tour communication: appointment details, material that helps couples picture a wedding at the venue, and an invitation to connect where that would be useful. Present this as a planning perspective, not a demonstrated improvement in attendance or bookings.",
    "cta": "Propose a LeadLock inquiry through the Reel's Instagram caption using DM keyword ADS. The email invites a reply about the owner's current pre-tour follow-up. Keep the Reel and carousel free of an explicit offer ask."
  },
